# Broker for the CI headless-CLI gate: one topic tree granted, everything else refused.
#
# A named user rather than anonymous, because a named user is what the gate's own
# identity check uses -- an anonymous connection here has to be rejected, and a broker
# that answers anyway is not this one. (`pattern` lines were once blamed for the gate
# seeing 0x10 instead of 0x87; measured on 2.0.11, 2.0.22 and 2.1.2 they do deny an
# anonymous client, so they were never the cause. See ITERATION 4.75.)
# The password itself is generated per job and never stored here.
user gateuser
topic readwrite cli-gate/#
